Gemma 4 describer weights — not tracked in git (see .gitignore)
=================================================================

The vision pipeline's describer (stage 4) loads the local vision-language model from:

    models/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit/

Expected contents: an MLX model directory (config.json, generation_config.json,
processor_config.json, chat_template.jinja, tokenizer.json, model.safetensors and
model.safetensors.index.json), 5.2 GB. It runs through MLX / mlx-vlm: Metal on Apple
silicon, CUDA on Linux with an NVIDIA GPU (see requirements.txt and requirements/).

Upstream source
---------------
Google Gemma 4 E4B, instruction-tuned (google/gemma-4-E4B-it), converted to 4-bit MLX
by mlx-community:

    https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit

LICENCE: the weights are licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/gemma_4_license) — NOT the MIT licence of this
repository's code, so the repository's licence does not cover them; anyone shipping them
does so under Apache 2.0's conditions. The mlx-community card's `license: gemma` tag looks
like converter boilerplate: upstream google/gemma-4-E4B-it is apache-2.0 (also at the
converted revision fee6332), and the Gemma Terms of Use exclude Gemma 4 (README > Licence
note). The app presents the model to the
operator as "JIC-AnyScan-v1" (see src/Vision/Core.py, CONST_MODEL_NAME, and
src/Vision/Describers.py, CONST_GEMMA_MODEL_DIR).

How to fetch
------------
With the Hugging Face CLI, `hf` (from huggingface_hub, in requirements.txt; the older
`huggingface-cli` no longer works). Public, no token needed. The revision is pinned to
the one the application was measured with — verified file by file against these weights:

    hf download mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit \
        --revision 475b9088d29754a3379866cf5aeb6b41acd313c2 \
        --local-dir models/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit

(models/florence2-large-ft/, the previous describer, is no longer used and can be
deleted.)


FastSAM instance-segmentation weights — not tracked in git
==========================================================

The vision pipeline's stage 2 loads FastSAM-x from:

    models/FastSAM/FastSAM-x.pt

Expected contents: the single 145 MB FastSAM-x.pt checkpoint.

Upstream source
---------------
Ultralytics FastSAM (AGPL-3.0 for the code; the weights are the published
FastSAM-x release):

    https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/fast-sam/

How to fetch
------------
Let ultralytics resolve and download the correct release, then move it into place
(version-robust — no pinned URL to rot):

    python -c "from ultralytics import FastSAM; FastSAM('FastSAM-x.pt')"
    mkdir -p models/FastSAM && mv FastSAM-x.pt models/FastSAM/

The pipeline resolves this path from Vision/Segmenter.py the same way the
describer's path is resolved (CONST_SEGMENTER_WEIGHTS); override it per run with
Example/Vision/analyze.py --weights.


DINOv2 identifier weights — not tracked in git
==============================================

The catalogue modes' identifier (Vision.Identifier) loads DINOv2 base from:

    models/dinov2-base/

Expected contents: README.md, config.json, preprocessor_config.json and
model.safetensors (346 MB). PyTorch, on the segmenter's device.

Upstream source
---------------
Meta's DINOv2, base size (ViT-B/14), at the revision the application was measured
with (2026-10-11):

    https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov2-base

LICENCE: Apache License 2.0 (the model card's tag at that revision) — not the MIT licence
of this repository's code.

How to fetch
------------
./install.sh downloads and verifies it. By hand:

    hf download facebook/dinov2-base README.md config.json preprocessor_config.json \
        model.safetensors --revision f9e44c814b77203eaa57a6bdbbd535f21ede1415 \
        --local-dir models/dinov2-base
